Error [E0209]: `eat` takes `v`, but `v` is used again later
  --> tests/ui/hardening/user_struct_named_noclone_is_still_cloneable.jet:12:9
    |
 12 |     eat(v)
    |         ^
  --> tests/ui/hardening/user_struct_named_noclone_is_still_cloneable.jet:13:13
    |
 13 |     print(v.n)
    |             ^ `v` is used again here
 Why: `eat` takes ownership of this argument; an unmarked argument moves only at its name's last use, and this is not the last use of `v`
 Fix: Write `v.copy()` to pass a copy and keep `v`, or reorder so this call is the last use of `v`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0209
